{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation in progress (worktree tok-30a2). Mechanism chosen: the ModelProfile capabilities seam (change 1014 / f184) is NOT on origin/main (feature branch only) and does not expose max output tokens, so the fallback applies: a per-model max-output table (MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS) beside sizing.largest_window_tokens — haiku-4-5: 64000, sonnet-4-6: 128000, opus-4-8: 128000, unknown -> DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS (16000). Applied via passes._max_output_cfg at all six bespoke builders (pass1_chunk incl. AGENT, pass1_container, pass1_isf, summarize_for_isf, pass2_completion, pass4_coach) + the prerequisite finder per-bin call (post-ladder-escalation), and via a new 'output_budget: model_max' with-input on the workflow verify (both arms), prerequisite-verifier, and coach steps (agentic verify keeps output_tokens_per_item as an additional floor-raiser for unmapped models). Bounded-recovery output_token_limit clamps untouched. Transport check: runner passes explicit per-request timeout (cfg.timeout_s) so the Anthropic SDK's large-max_tokens streaming guard does not fire; wall-clock bound unchanged. New tests: tests/unit/workflow/test_plan_review_output_budget.py (16 passing); lint+typecheck+workflow suite green."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785478507478331001,"uuid":"e5a764e7-7ed9-4d4e-9b7b-69f56e7d0239"}